{"chunk_id": "68202c163669", "text": "After Hanuman kills the young titan prince Aksha, the shaken yet calculating Ravana sends his greatest warrior\u2014his son Indrajita\u2014to confront the invincible monkey. Ravana warns that ordinary armies and weapons cannot defeat Hanuman, whose speed and power resemble fire itself. Indrajita rides out in a celestial chariot drawn by lions, and the clash becomes a spectacular aerial duel: arrows streak like lightning while Hanuman twists and darts through the sky with supernatural agility. Realizing Hanuman cannot be slain, Indrajita uses the sacred Brahma\u2011weapon to bind him. Though struck down, Hanuman remembers Brahma\u2019s boon and deliberately submits, recognizing a strategic opportunity: capture will bring him face to face with Ravana. Feigning helplessness, he allows the demons to bind and parade him through Lanka until he is brought before the titan king, where he finally declares himself the messenger of Sugriva.\nAfter Aksha\u2019s death, Indrajit battles Hanuman, binds him with the Brahma weapon, and Hanuman deliberately allows capture to gain audience with Ravana.\nThemes: strategic surrender, divine weapons, warfare and valor, loyalty to Rama, encounter with Ravana", "vector": [-0.005106284283101559, -0.027727529406547546, -0.017582325264811516, 0.009417659603059292, 0.009060623124241829, 0.024440106004476547, -0.03015267662703991, -0.009666910395026207, -0.01760927028954029, -0.015803882852196693, 0.0013161482056602836, 0.011088317260146141, 0.014591309241950512, 0.0035097284708172083, 0.002561562927439809, 0.005106284283101559, 0.040526922792196274, -0.013971548527479172, 0.027889205142855644, -0.023806871846318245, -0.007976043038070202, -0.013769453391432762, -0.01224026270210743, 0.014874243177473545, -0.028050880879163742, 0.011068107560276985, 0.019320348277688026, -0.030287407338619232, 0.021758969873189926, -0.02078890986740589, 0.006931882351636887, -0.012529932893812656, -0.005298275500535965, -0.